{"id":"vanished","title":"Paid millions, then gone from the ledger","question":"Which payees received large sums and then stopped being paid altogether, and did a similar newcomer appear in the same department the following year?","finding":"101 payees that received $5 million or more since fiscal 2019 ($2.84 billion together) have no payment of any kind after fiscal 2024. The largest are Tutor Perini Corporation ($598.4 million, last paid fiscal 2023), Goodwill SF Urban Development LLC ($236.5 million, last paid fiscal 2023), Skanska Constructors ($141.2 million, last paid fiscal 2021). 18 were paid mostly or wholly under emergency powers, 15 of them last paid in fiscal 2021 to 2023. 33 carry a warning sign elsewhere in this project. For 2 a newcomer sharing a distinctive word of the name was first paid by the same department, for the same purpose, the next year (Arthur J Gallagher & Co Ins Brk Of Calif then Arthur J. Gallagher Risk Mgmt Svcs LLC; 350 Rhode Island Operating Company LLC then KAIM 350 Rhode Island LLC); for 14 more a newcomer without a shared name was paid a similar amount. Each is a lead to check, not a match.","how":"A payee is listed when its outside-spending payments from fiscal 2019 to 2026 total $5 million or more and no payment of any kind was issued to it in fiscal 2025, 2026 or 2027 to date. The year a payment was issued is read from its voucher number, not from the year the file lists it under: a line filed under fiscal 2025 for a payment issued years before does not keep a payee in the ledger, and a payee whose every payment was issued before fiscal 2019 is not listed. For each, the same department’s payees of the following year are searched for one first paid in that year or the year before, paid for the same purpose, and either sharing a distinctive word of the name (amount within a third to three times) or paid within a quarter of the vanished payee’s last full-year amount. Rows with a shared-name newcomer come first, then rows with a warning sign or a similar-amount newcomer, then by total.","limits":"Most payees stop for plain reasons: a construction project is finished, a joint venture formed for it is wound up, a lease ends, a building is bought outright in one payment, an emergency hotel programme closes, a firm is bought and trades under the buyer’s name. A newcomer with a similar name is often the same landlord or insurer under a new legal entity, which is ordinary. A newcomer paid a similar amount may simply have won the next competition. What would settle a row: the Secretary of State’s business filings for both names, and the contract assignment or new solicitation on file with the department. The payment file labels each line with a fiscal year that is not always the year the payment was issued: some earlier payments, mostly on purchase orders in multi-year capital funds, are filed under a later year, and the Controller's own published figures follow that label. Payments are dated here by voucher number, a single running sequence, which moves $5.52 billion of $119.3 billion (4.6%) to an earlier year than its label; $1.08 billion of that belongs to fiscal 2018 or earlier, before the file starts. Near the turn of a year the number dates a payment to within a few days. The $992.6 million of outside spending that belongs to fiscal 2018 or earlier is in none of the figures here; it is used only to tell that a payee is not new.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"payee","t":"Payee","type":"org"},{"k":"total","t":"Paid, fiscal 2019–2026","type":"usd"},{"k":"lastYear","t":"Last fiscal year paid","type":"year"},{"k":"lastPaid","t":"Paid that year","type":"usd"},{"k":"peakYear","t":"Peak year","type":"year"},{"k":"peakPaid","t":"Paid at peak","type":"usd"},{"k":"department","t":"Main department","type":"text"},{"k":"what","t":"Mostly paid for","type":"text"},{"k":"awarded","t":"How awarded","type":"text"},{"k":"signs","t":"Warning signs elsewhere","type":"int"},{"k":"sign","t":"First warning sign","type":"text"},{"k":"newcomer","t":"Newcomer the next year","type":"org"},{"k":"newcomerPaid","t":"Paid to the newcomer that year","type":"usd"},{"k":"basis","t":"Why it is shown","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"total":33358945,"lastYear":"2024","lastPaid":13332300,"peakYear":"2024","peakPaid":13332300,"department":"City Administrator","what":"Insurance expense","awarded":"all under a rule that does not say","signs":0,"sign":"","newcomerPaid":17678304,"basis":"lead to check, not a match: first paid in fiscal 2025, same department and purpose, shares the words Arthur Gallagher","payee":"Arthur J Gallagher & Co Ins Brk Of Calif","payeeKey":null,"newcomer":"Arthur J. Gallagher Risk Mgmt Svcs LLC","newcomerKey":null},{"total":19194085,"lastYear":"2022","lastPaid":5689637,"peakYear":"2021","peakPaid":10567667,"department":"City Administrator","what":"Property rent","awarded":"all under a rule that does not say","signs":1,"sign":"Lead: Registered 2019-11-25 and paid $13.5 million within two fiscal years.","newcomerPaid":8217270,"basis":"lead to check, not a match: first paid in fiscal 2022, same department and purpose, shares the words 350 Rhode Island","payee":"350 Rhode Island Operating Company LLC","payeeKey":null,"newcomer":"KAIM 350 Rhode Island LLC","newcomerKey":null},{"total":98308320,"lastYear":"2021","lastPaid":591324,"peakYear":"2019","peakPaid":73547424,"department":"Airport Commission","what":"Building structures improvements direct purchase","awarded":"all competed","signs":1,"sign":"Lead: The files tie it to another City payee, Aecom Technical Services Inc. (named as trade name, parent or related organization in a filing): $123.1 million paid to this","newcomerPaid":26494872,"basis":"lead to check, not a match: first paid in fiscal 2021, same department and purpose, similar amount, no shared name","payee":"Hunt Construction Group Inc","payeeKey":null,"newcomer":"Mccarthy Building Companies Inc","newcomerKey":null},{"total":85709651,"lastYear":"2023","lastPaid":2